    {v_1 : int ⊎ float} |= v_1 ≠ 0

[Example Rules]
Rule 13 (tensor must have a floating-point dtype: 6–8)
{v1: tensor} |= 6 ≤ dtype(v1) ∧ dtype(v1) ≤ 8

Rule 32 (Integer indices only valid with int-compatible dtype)
{v_1 : tuple(int), v_2 : dtype} |= ∀i ∈ [0, v_1.len - 1] : v_1[i] ≥ 0 ∧ v_2 = 1 ∨ v_2 = 2 ∨ v_2 = 3 ∨ v_2 = 4 ∨ v_2 = 5

Rule 1 (tensor shapes should be the same)
{v_1 : tensor, v_2 : tensor} |= ndim(v_1) = ndim(v_2) ∧ ∀i ∈ [0, ndim(v_1) − 1] : shape(v_1, i) = shape(v_2, i)

Rule 6 (last dimension of a tensor matches first dimension of the other)
{v_1 : tensor, v_2 : tensor} |= ndim(v_1) > 0 ∧ ndim(v_2) > 0 ∧ shape(v_1, ndim(v_1) − 1) = shape(v_2, 0)

Rule 27 (reduction over valid dimensions)
{v_1 : tensor, v_2 : tuple(int)} |= ∀i ∈ [0, v_2.len - 1] : 0 ≤ v_2[i] ∧ v_2[i] < ndim(v_1)

